    "body": "Closes #120.\n\nImplements ADR-014. Before this, an unstyled HTML page renders as a text dump: `<h1>` is 16px (same as `<p>`), no paragraph gap, no body inset. This commit gives every unstyled page its expected defaults and makes the cascade origin-aware.\n\n## What changed\n\n**1. UA stylesheet module** (new files: `src/renderer/css/ua_stylesheet.{hpp,cpp}`)\n\n13 rules parsed once from a string constant, cached in a function-local static. Content per ADR-014:\n\n- `body { margin: 8px }`\n- `h1..h6` with font-size (2em down to 0.67em), bold, and per-level margins\n- `p { margin: 1em 0 }`\n- `em/i/cite/var/address { font-style: italic }`\n- `strong/b { font-weight: bold }`\n- `code/pre/kbd/samp/tt { font-family: monospace }`\n- `ul/ol { margin: 1em 0; padding-left: 40px }`\n- `a { color: #0000EE }`\n\n`font-weight` and `font-style` are declared so the sheet matches CSS 2.1's intent. They cascade correctly but don't yet flow into `LayoutText` (that's the future font-metrics ADR).\n\n**2. Origin-aware cascade** (`cascade.{hpp,cpp}`)\n\n- New `enum class Origin { UserAgent, Author }`.\n- `CascadeValue` gains `Origin origin`, default `Author`.\n- `beats()` gains origin as a tiebreaker after importance and before specificity, per CSS 2.1 §6.4.1.\n- New two-sheet overload: `cascade(ua_sheet, author_sheet, doc)`.\n- Old single-sheet overload kept; delegates with an empty UA sheet so existing callers and tests compile unchanged.\n\n**3. Pipeline wiring** (`render_pipeline.cpp`)\n\nOne-line change: `cascade(ua_stylesheet(), sheet, *doc_)`.\n\n**4. CMake** (2 lines)\n\n## Why origin-aware, not concatenation\n\nThe naive implementation is `Stylesheet::parse(ua_css + author_css)`. This breaks on:\n\n- UA: `h1 { color: navy }` (specificity 0,0,1)\n- Author: `* { color: red }` (specificity 0,0,0)\n\nConcatenation keeps h1 navy because `beats()` checks specificity first. Origin-aware makes it red because author origin beats UA origin before specificity. This is the CSS 2.1 §6.4.1 rule, and it matters in practice for any author CSS reset using `*`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `[ua_stylesheet]` -> 7 cases, 17 assertions, all pass\n- `[css][cascade]` -> 17 cases, 35 assertions (13 existing + 4 new origin tests), all pass\n- Full suite -> 165 cases, 669 assertions, all pass (was 154/644 before)\n- `grep -rl \"lexbor/\" src/` still returns exactly `src/renderer/html/convert.cpp`\n- No changes to `renderer::dom`, `renderer::layout`, `renderer::paint`, `renderer::html`, or `renderer::css` selectors/stylesheet\n\n## Visible effect\n\nWelcome page (`<h1>` + three `<p>` lines, zero author CSS):\n\n- Before: h1 at 16px, no gaps, no body inset -- text dump\n- After: h1 at 32px, paragraph gaps, 8px body inset -- a document\n\nDemo page (`docs/demo.html`, has author CSS): renders identically to before -- author overrides UA at every property it declares, which is the expected origin-aware behavior.\n\n## Deferred (per ADR-014)\n\n- `display: inline` / `display: none` (layout is block-only)\n- Retiring the `<head>` skip list (needs `display: none`)\n- Table and form elements\n- `text-decoration: underline` on links (paint doesn't support it)\n- Pseudo-class selectors (`a:link`, `a:visited`)\n- UA `!important` rules\n- Full CSS 2.1 UA stylesheet (~100 rules)\n\n## Next\n\nADR-015: inline formatting. The biggest remaining structural gap -- `<span>`, `<a>`, `<em>` currently render as blocks and text doesn't wrap. That's what turns v0.2.0 into a browser that renders paragraphs the way their authors wrote them.\n",
